# preferred-citation points to the ZfdG article that references teiCrafter, the
# base of this tool; it is a field survey rather than a paper solely about this
# software, used here per the maintainer's stated citation preference.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use wenzelsbibel-teiCrafter in academic work, please cite the
  preferred-citation (the ZfdG article). To cite the software itself, use the
  metadata below.
title: wenzelsbibel-teiCrafter
abstract: >-
  Editing environment for the Wenzelsbibel edition (Codex 2759), derived from
  teiCrafter. It keeps the raw TEI string canonical, edits by offset splices
  and writes byte-identical output outside the edit, and adds the project's
  editorial layer, registers, image annotations and IIIF facsimiles.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Pollin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4879-129X"
    affiliation: "Digital Humanities Craft OG"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DigitalHumanitiesCraft/wenzelsbibel-teiCrafter"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - TEI
  - TEI-XML
  - digital scholarly editing
  - text encoding
  - Wenzelsbibel
  - Codex 2759
# No release is tagged yet; version and date-released follow the first release.
